drm/omap: RFBI output and Epson S1D1374x controller (Nokia N800/N810 display)

The N800/N810 display is DISPC -> RFBI -> Epson S1D13745 ('Blizzard'),
a controller with its own frame memory driving the 800x480 panel. omapdrm
lost RFBI in 2017 (aa61321d4c08 'drm/omap: remove rfbi'), and the N8x0
have had no display since the old omapfb's OMAP2 support went in 3.4.

- dss/rfbi.c: RFBI as an omapdss output (OMAP_DSS_OUTPUT_DBI on the LCD
  channel), manually updated through the same hooks as DSI command mode:
  DISPC in stall mode with the RFBI pad mode; per update the client sets
  up the controller over the bus (8 bits per cycle), then RFBI is armed
  (ITE, 16 bits per cycle) and DISPC sends one frame (FRAMEDONE).
  Bootloader bus timings are kept. Exports a small bus API (command,
  data, read) for the controller driver.
- dss/s1d1374x.c: the controller as the next bridge: before each update
  sets its input/output window, RGB565 input and data source, leaving
  the register index at the memory data port; identifies S1D13744 vs
  S1D13745; provides the 800x480 mode. PLL, SDRAM and panel stay as the
  bootloader (NOLO) set them.
- fbdev: RGB565 when the display is on RFBI (the bus is 16 bits; Maemo
  expects RGB565); the fbdev probe no longer forces 32 bpp over that.
- DT (n8x0): enable dss and rfbi, add the controller and the graph.

Sequence after Nokia's omapfb blizzard.c/rfbi.c/dispc.c.
